{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`src/rebar/_deprecations.py:94-112` schedules three public removals: the Python-library `rebar.transition(force_close=...)` keyword, boolean `rebar.transition(force=True)`, and explicit hosted-OpenAI `openai-chat:` model selection. Closed migration `blusterous-earthly-kitten` established the temporary warning mappings; this ticket is the scheduled retirement, not a duplicate of that migration. The CLI already rejects retired close spellings in `src/rebar/_commands/transition.py`. The MCP transition schema never exposed `force_close`.\n\n## End State\n\nThe Python library accepts only a reason-bearing string `force=\"<reason>\"`. `force_close` or boolean `force=True` fail at the library boundary with `force=\"<reason>\"` named as the replacement. Hosted model selection accepts `openai-responses:<model>`. Both live hosted-resolution paths reject explicit `openai-chat:`. Custom OpenAI-compatible `base_url` selection retains its Chat Completions dialect.\n\n## Implementation Plan\n\n1. Retire the two library mappings in `_lib_writes` plus `_deprecations`. Do not add an environment or configuration tombstone: these are callable inputs, so validation belongs at the Python boundary.\n2. Regenerate the API snapshot plus MCP-library parity manifest after the library signature changes.\n3. Retire hosted explicit `openai-chat:` in both resolver clusters: `_resolve_target` plus `_pai_model`/`_openai_wire_prefix`. Preserve the custom-endpoint branch. Migrate the hosted `gpt-5.4*` provider inventory to `openai-responses:`.\n4. Regenerate `docs/config-reference.md` through `scripts/gen_config_reference.py` after the cfg-kind deprecation row is removed.\n5. Replace the two legacy warn-and-map tests in `test_force_unification_blusterous.py` with library-rejection tests. Retarget every behavior-preserving public test caller to `force=\"<reason>\"`: `test_completion_gate.py`, `test_ac_checkbox_precheck_heldout.py`, `test_attestations_integration.py`, `test_plan_review_close_gate_lifecycle.py`, `test_attested_close_guard_e2e.py`, and `test_transition_open_children.py`.\n6. Update maintained documentation plus generated references. Preserve historical `force_close_reason` durable state.\n7. Add focused boundary, resolver, provider, manifest, and documentation-generation regression coverage.\n\n## File Impact\n\n- `src/rebar/_deprecations.py`, `src/rebar/_lib_writes.py` — retired library inputs\n- `tests/unit/api_surface_baseline.json`, `scripts/gen_api_surface.py` — generated public API signature snapshot\n- `tests/unit/mcp_library_parity_manifest.json`, `scripts/check_mcp_library_parity.py` — retired library-only parity divergence\n- `src/rebar/llm/runner.py`, `src/rebar/llm/model_classes.py`, `src/rebar/llm/anthropic_model.py`, `src/rebar/llm/config.py`, `.github/llm-providers/openai.toml` — both hosted model-resolution paths plus deployed model inventory\n- `docs/config-reference.md`, `scripts/gen_config_reference.py`, `tests/unit/test_gen_config_reference.py` — cfg-kind deprecation output\n- `tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_force_unification_blusterous.py`, `test_completion_gate.py`, `test_ac_checkbox_precheck_heldout.py`, `test_attestations_integration.py`, `test_plan_review_close_gate_lifecycle.py`, `test_attested_close_guard_e2e.py`, `test_transition_open_children.py` — rejection migration plus canonical public-callers\n- maintained API/provider docs, generated references, `CHANGELOG.md`, `docs/release-notes.md` — replacement guidance\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `rebar.transition(force_close=\"legacy\")` is rejected at the Python-library boundary. Its error names `force=\"<explicit reason>\"`.\n- [ ] `rebar.transition(force=True)` is rejected at the Python-library boundary. Its error names `force=\"<explicit reason>\"`.\n- [ ] `rebar.transition(force=\"approved reason\")` remains accepted.\n- [ ] `tests/unit/api_surface_baseline.json` is regenerated through `scripts/gen_api_surface.py`. Its `transition` signature has no `force_close` row.\n- [ ] `tests/unit/mcp_library_parity_manifest.json` removes the retired `force_close` divergence.\n- [ ] `tests/unit/mcp_library_parity_manifest.json` removes the retired `force_close` `library_params` entry.\n- [ ] `scripts/check_mcp_library_parity.py` passes.\n- [ ] The CLI retains its existing retired-input rejection. This ticket adds no CLI force-close removal.\n- [ ] The MCP transition schema remains free of `force_close`. This ticket adds no MCP force-close removal.\n- [ ] Explicit hosted `openai-chat:gpt-5.4` is rejected through `_resolve_target`. Its error names `openai-responses:gpt-5.4`.\n- [ ] Explicit hosted `openai-chat:gpt-5.4` is rejected through `_pai_model`. Its error names `openai-responses:gpt-5.4`.\n- [ ] Explicit hosted `openai-responses:gpt-5.4` succeeds.\n- [ ] Each hosted `gpt-5.4*` entry in `.github/llm-providers/openai.toml` uses `openai-responses:`.\n- [ ] A custom OpenAI-compatible `base_url` retains Chat Completions routing.\n- [ ] `scripts/gen_config_reference.py --check` passes with the retired hosted-OpenAI cfg row absent from `docs/config-reference.md`.\n- [ ] `test_force_unification_blusterous.py` has no test that expects warning-plus-mapping from `force_close` or boolean `force`.\n- [ ] Every listed behavior-preserving lifecycle caller uses the canonical `force=\"<reason>\"` form.\n- [ ] The reviewed public-call scan leaves legacy `force_close` or boolean-force spelling only in explicit negative rejection tests or historical durable-state coverage.\n- [ ] Maintained documentation names the canonical replacements. Historical durable `force_close_reason` state remains intact.\n- [ ] Focused boundary checks pass.\n- [ ] Focused resolver checks pass.\n- [ ] Focused provider checks pass.\n- [ ] Generated-reference checks pass.\n- [ ] Lint passes.\n- [ ] Typecheck passes."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788370025335092001,"uuid":"023dfb35-9250-44f8-89db-2aa7cf16b362"}